<title>CHINA: Shangri-La forms group for loan.</title>
<headline>Shangri-La forms group for loan.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shangri-La Asia Ltd has formed an arranger group for its US$500 million five-year revolving loan/term facility launched on Monday, bankers said.</p>
<p>Because of oversubscription, the commitments of the 17 arrangers had been scaled back, bankers said.</p>
<p>The facility carries an annual interest margin of 0.53 percent, with a three-year revolving period, after which the outstanding amount converts to a term loan, they said.</p>
<p>HSBC Investment Bank Asia Ltd, J.P. Morgan Securities Asia Ltd and Societe Generale Asia Ltd are coordinating arrangers.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6321</p>
